window.docContents[186].resolve({"/Foundations/#PDEAtlas--Foundations--Coordinates-and-Boundary-Calculus--Boundary-Calculus-and-C___-Boundary-Geometry--Scope___-dimensions___-and-orientation-conventions":{"contents":"The box theorem is formulated in dimension . This presentation gives a\nnonempty coordinate type without carrying a separate positivity assumption.\nThe endpoints satisfy the coordinatewise non-strict inequality .\nConsequently, degenerate boxes and degenerate rectangles are included.\n\nThe ball theorems are formulated in dimension  with the explicit typeclass\nassumption , and the radius hypothesis is strict: . Ball integrals\nuse the open metric ball. Sphere integrals use the library's sphere measure.\n\nFor operational C¹ domains, every chart sends the physical domain to the\npositive side of the flattened last coordinate:\n\n\n\ninside the chart source. Therefore decreasing flattened height points outward.\nThis sign convention determines the minus sign in the chartwise normal.\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Foundations\u0009Coordinates and Boundary Calculus\u0009Boundary Calculus and C¹ Boundary Geometry","header":"3.3.2.1. Scope, dimensions, and orientation conventions","id":"/Foundations/#PDEAtlas--Foundations--Coordinates-and-Boundary-Calculus--Boundary-Calculus-and-C___-Boundary-Geometry--Scope___-dimensions___-and-orientation-conventions"},"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev___-Morrey___-Poincar______-and-Hardy--Integrability":{"contents":"For , the first-order whole-space theorem reaches\n.  Higher-order subcritical results iterate the first-order\nstep while . On a bounded operational  domain this gives a\nbounded linear inclusion\n\n\n\nThe map preserves every retained weak derivative. Its norm is bounded by\na product of first-order GNS constants, extension norms, and the finite\ncoordinate counts in the graph norm. Only first-order extension is used,\neven when several derivatives are consumed.\n\nAt the critical exponent, a bounded operational  domain admits the\nbounded linear inclusion\n\n\n\nEvery retained derivative agrees almost everywhere with the source. The\noperator estimate combines the subcritical steps with a final critical\nfirst-order estimate, and its constant depends on . This does not give\nan  embedding in dimensions greater than one.\n\n","context":"PDEAtlas\u0009Sobolev Spaces and Weak Derivatives\u0009Coverage and Open Problems\u0009Sobolev Coverage and Open Problems\u0009Sobolev, Morrey, Poincaré, and Hardy","header":"4.6.1.6.1. Integrability","id":"/Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives/#PDEAtlas--Sobolev-Spaces-and-Weak-Derivatives--Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev-Coverage-and-Open-Problems--Sobolev___-Morrey___-Poincar______-and-Hardy--Integrability"}});